The stages before a forced one must be up to date, and the run stops instead of running them, because on a film they are the expensive ones (2 h of separation, up to an hour of transcription): a typo'd setting or a deleted file would otherwise start hours of work the user asked to skip. state.json keeps only a fingerprint hash, so the message can't name the changed setting; it says the settings or the video changed. Considered a separate --from-stage flag; extending --force kept one flag for 'redo', with plain --force unchanged. The Pipeline's force= parameter was dropped since from_stage of the first stage does the same.
